  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#mapping_id_1",
  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The man is mapped as the embodiment of someone who 'earns' things through hard work.",
  "description": "The text 'if you want something get off your ass and earn it' implicitly maps the visual entity 'man' as the archetype of someone who achieves goals through effort. The man's posture (leaning against hay bales, hand on hip) and setting (rural field) visually reinforce the stereotype of a hardworking rural American worker, which is then used to represent the ideal person who 'earns' things. This mapping is supported by the background knowledge entities 'rural_american_worker_stereotype' and 'self_reliance_philosophy'. The text's message is made concrete by projecting the visual of the man onto the abstract concept of 'earning' through action.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
  "extractedFrom": "80672",
